{"r":"xnq","lane":{"p":818,"e":[{"h":"خَنَقَهُ","t":["(S, Mgh, Msb, K,) aor. , (S, Msb,) inf. n. ",[2,"خَنِقٌ"]," (S Mgh, Msb, K) and ",[2,"خَنْقٌ"],", (Msb, TA,) the latter a contraction of the former, (Msb,) or, accord. to El-Fárábee, the latter is not allowable, (Mgh,) ",[1,"He throttled him,"]," or ",[1,"strangled him,"]," i. e. ",[1,"squeezed his throat"]," (Mgh, Msb) ",[1,"that he might die;"]," (Msb;) [but it does not always mean ",[1,"he squeezed his throat so that he died;"]," often meaning, simply, ",[1,"he,"]," or ",[1,"it, throttled him, strangled him,"]," or ",[1,"choked him;"]," and frequently said of a disease in the throat, and of food;] and ↓ ",[2,"خنّقهُ"]," signifies the same, (S, K,) [or has an intensive meaning,] and its inf. n. is ",[2,"تَخْنِيقٌ"],". (TA.) ― -b2- [Hence,] ",[2,"العَبْرَةُ"]," ↓ ",[2,"خَنَّقَتْهُ"]," [and ",[2,"خَنَقَتْهُ"],"] (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"Weeping"]," [or ",[1,"sobbing"],"] ",[1,"choked him;"]," as though the tears throttled him. (Mgh.) ― -b3- And ",[2,"خُنِقَ"],[1,"He"]," (a horse) ",[1,"was affected with the disease,"]," or ",[1,"wind in the throat, termed"],[2,"خُنَاقِيَّة"],". (TA.) ― -b4- And ",[2,"خَنَقَ الوَقْتَ"],", aor. as above, (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He postponed,"]," or ",[1,"deferred, and"]," [",[1,"so"],"] ",[1,"straitened, the time:"]," and ",[2,"خَنَقَ الصَّلَاةَ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He straitened the time of prayer by postponing it,"]," or ",[1,"deferring it."]," (TA.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"خَنَّقَ","t":["see 1, in two places. ― -b2- You say also, ",[2,"خنّق السَّرَابُ الجِبَالَ"],", inf. n. ",[2,"تَخْنِيقٌ"],", (tropical:) ",[1,"The mirage nearly covered the heads of the mountains."]," (K, TA.) ― -b3- And ",[2,"خنّق الإِنَآءَ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"He filled the vessel:"]," (K, TA:) or ",[1,"filled it up"]," (",[2,"سَدَّدَ مَلْأَهُ"],"): and in like manner, ",[2,"الحَوْضَ"]," [",[1,"the watering-trough"],"]. (Aboo-Sa'eed, TA.) ― -b4- And ",[2,"خنّق الأَرْبَعِينَ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"He"]," (a man) ",[1,"nearly attained to"]," [the age of] ",[1,"forty"]," [years]. (K, TA.)"],"f":"2"},{"h":"إِنْخَنَقَ","t":["see what next follows, in three places."],"f":"7"},{"h":"اختنق","t":[[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, throttled,"]," or ",[1,"strangled;"]," i. e. ",[1,"he had his throat squeezed that he might die;"]," (JK, * S, * Msb, K; *) [and simply ",[1,"he was,"]," or ",[1,"became, throttled, strangled,"]," or ",[1,"choked;"],"] as also ↓ ",[2,"انخنق"],": (JK, * Msb:) or you say, ↓ ",[2,"انخنقت"],[2,"الشَّاةُ بِنَفْسِهَا"]," [",[1,"the sheep,"]," or ",[1,"goat, became throttled,"]," or ",[1,"strangled,"]," or ",[1,"choked, by itself"],"]: (S, K:) or ↓ ",[2,"الاِنْخِنَاقُ"]," signifies ",[1,"the having the"],[2,"خِنَاق"]," [q. v.] ",[1,"compressed upon one's throat:"]," and ",[2,"الاِخْتِنَاقُ"],", ",[1,"the compressing it upon one's own throat."]," (TA.)"],"f":"8"},{"h":"خَنْقٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"مُخَنَّقٌ"],"."]},{"h":"خَنِقٌ","t":["inf. n. of ",[2,"خَنَقَهُ"],": (S, Mgh, Msb, K:) -A2- and ",[1,"i. q."],[2,"مَخْنُوقٌ"]," q. v. (JK, K.)"]},{"h":"خُنُقٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"خِنَاقٌ"],"."]},{"h":"خُنِاقٌ","t":["[",[1,"Quinsy;"],"] ",[1,"a certain disease which pre vents the passage of the breath to the lungs and heart;"]," (K;) as also [↓ ",[2,"خُنَاقَةٌ"]," thus in modern Arabic, and] ↓ ",[2,"خُنَّاقٌ"],": pl. ",[2,"خَوَانِيقُ"]," (TA) [and ",[2,"خَنَّانِيقُ"],", thus in modern Arabic]. ― -b2- See also ",[2,"مُخَنَّقٌ"],", in three places."]},{"h":"خِنَاقٌ","t":[[1,"A cord,"]," (JK, S, Mgh, K,) or ",[1,"bow-string,"]," or ",[1,"the like,"]," (Mgh,) ",[1,"with which one is strangled;"]," (JK, * S, * Mgh, K; *) also, metaphorically, termed ",[2,"خَنَّاقٍ"]," ↓ ",[2,"مِخْنَقَةُ"],". (Mgh.) ― -b2- See also ",[2,"مُخَنَّقٌ"],", in two places. ― -b3- ",[2,"فَلْهَمٌ خِنَاقٌ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A narrow vulva of a woman:"]," (Abu-l-'Abbás, TA:) and ↓ ",[2,"خُنُقٌ"]," [or ",[2,"فُرُوجُ خُنُقٌ"],", for ",[2,"خُنُقٌ"]," is app. pl. of ",[2,"خِنَاقٌ"],", like as ",[2,"كُنُزٌ"]," is pl. of ",[2,"كِنَازٌ"],",] (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"narrow vulvas"]," (IAar, K) ",[1,"of women."]," (IAar.) ― -b4- ",[2,"هُمْ فِى خِنَاقٍ مِنَ المَوْتِ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"They are in straitness by reason of death."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"خَنِيقٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"مَخْنُوقٌ"],", in three places."]},{"h":"خُنَاقَةٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"خُنَاقٌ"],"."]},{"h":"خُنَاقِيَّةٌ","t":[[1,"A certain disease in the throats of birds and horses:"]," (K:) or ",[1,"a certain disease that attacks the bird in its head,"]," and ",[1,"the horse in its throat, and chokes it:"]," (JK:) or ",[1,"a certain disease,"]," or ",[1,"wind, that attacks men and horses or similar beasts in the throat, and sometimes attacks birds in the head and throat, mostly appearing in pigeons."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"خَنَّاقٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"خَانِقٌ"],". ― -b2- Also One ",[1,"who sells fish"]," [",[1,"taken"],"] ",[1,"with the"],[2,"خَنَّاقَة"]," [q. v.]. (TA.)"]},{"h":"خُنَّاقٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"خُنَاقٌ"],"."]},{"h":"خَنَّاقَةٌ","t":[[1,"A snare with which beasts of prey are taken"]," (JK, TA) ",[1,"by the throat:"]," and ",[1,"a snare with which fish are taken in El-Andalus."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"خَانِقٌ","t":["One ",[1,"who strangles;"]," (Msb, TA; *) as also ↓ ",[2,"خَنَّاقٌ"],": (Mgh, Msb:) or the latter signifies one ",[1,"whose office it is to strangle."]," (TA.) ― -b2- [Hence,] ",[2,"خَانِقُ الذِّئْبِ"]," and ",[2,"خَانِقُ النَّمِرِ"]," and ",[2,"خَانِقُ"],[2,"الكَلْبِ"]," and ",[2,"خَانِقُ الكِرْسَنَّةِ"]," [in the CK ",[2,"الكَرْسَنَّةُ"],"] Four ",[1,"herbs:"]," (K:) [the first and second, in the present day, ",[1,"wolfsbane,"]," or ",[1,"aconite:"]," or, as Golius says, referring for the former and latter respectively to Diosc. iv. 78 and 77, the former is the ",[1,"aconitum lycoctonon;"]," and the latter, the ",[1,"aconitum pardalianches:"]," the third, ",[1,"dogsbane,"]," or ",[1,"colchicum;"]," or, as Golius says, referring to Diosc. iv. 81, ",[1,"apocynon:"]," and the fourth, ",[1,"strangle-weed,"]," (because it strangles the ",[2,"كِرْسَنَّة"],", or bitter vetch,) or ",[1,"broomrape,"]," i. e., as Golius says, referring to Diosc. ii. 172 and Ibn-Beytár, ",[1,"orobanche:"],"] the first is ",[1,"high"]," (",[2,"مشرف"]," [but perhaps this should be ",[2,"مُشْرِق"]," i. e. ",[1,"shining"],"]) ",[1,"in the leaves, downy, and resembling the"],[2,"دلب"]," [?]: the second is ",[1,"like the tail of the scorpion, glistening, about a span"]," [",[1,"in height"],"], ",[1,"and has not more than five leaves: each of these is of the"]," [",[1,"season called"],"] ",[2,"رَبِيع"],"; ",[1,"and they are poisonous; they kill all animals;"]," the ",[2,"ذِئْب"]," and the ",[2,"نَمِر"]," being particularized only because of the quickness of its acting in them: Ibn-Seenà says, in the “ Kánoon, ” the leaves of ",[2,"خانق النمر"],", when mixed with fat, and kneaded and baked with bread, and given as food to wolves and dogs and foxes and leopards (",[2,"نمر"],"), kills them: whence it seems that this may be two herbs or one herb. (TA.) ― -b3- ",[2,"خَانِقٌ"]," signifies also (tropical:) ",[1,"A narrow road"]," or ",[1,"ravine, in a mountain:"]," (S, * K, * TA:) or ",[1,"a narrow place"]," or ",[1,"pass, between two mountains,"]," and ",[1,"between two tracts of sand."]," (JK.) [See also ",[2,"مُخْتَنَقٌ"],".] ― -b4- And (tropical:) ",[1,"A narrow street;"]," syn. ",[2,"زُقَاقٌ"],"; (S, K, TA;) in the dial. of the people of ElYemen. (S, TA.) ― -b5- See also ",[2,"مَخْنُوقٌ"],", in two places."]},{"h":"خَانَقَاهٌ","t":[[1,"A convent inhabited by righteous and good men, and Soofees;"]," an arabicized word, from [the Persian] ",[2,"خَانَهْ گَاهْ"],"; [and post-classical, for] El-Makreezee says that the ",[2,"خانقاه"]," was instituted in the fifth century of the Flight, for Soofee recluses to employ themselves therein in the service of God: (TA:) [pl. ",[2,"خَوَانِقُ"],".]"]},{"h":"خَاَنقَاهِىٌّ","t":["A man ",[1,"of,"]," or ",[1,"belonging to, a"],[2,"خَانَقَاه"],". (TA.)"]},{"h":"مَخْنَقٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"مُخَنَّقٌ"],", in two places."]},{"h":"مِخْنَقَةٌ","t":[[1,"A necklace,"]," syn. ",[2,"قِلَادَةٌ"],", (S, Mgh, Msb, K,) ",[1,"that surrounds the neck;"]," (Mgh, Msb;) wherefore it is thus called; (Msb;) [i. e., because] ",[1,"it lies against the"],[2,"مُخَنَّق"],": pl. ",[2,"مَخَانِقُ"],". (TA.) ― -b2- See also ",[2,"خِنَاقٌ"],". [And see ",[2,"زِرَادٌ"],".]"]},{"h":"مُخَنَّقٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"مَخْنُوقٌ"],". ― -b2- [Hence,] ",[2,"غُلَامٌ مُخَنَّقُ"],[2,"الخَصْرِ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A boy slender in the waist."]," (K.) -A2- Also The ",[1,"part, of the neck, which is the place of the cord"]," [or ",[1,"the like"],"] ",[1,"called"],[2,"خِنَاق"]," [",[1,"wherewith one is strangled"],"]; (S, K; *) i. e., (TA,) the ",[1,"throat;"]," (K, accord. to the TA; in the CK and in my MS. copy of the K ↓ ",[2,"مَخْنَق"],";) and so ↓ ",[2,"خُنَاقٌ"],", (S, K, in the former said to be syn. with ",[2,"مُخَنَّقٌ"],",) and ↓ ",[2,"خِنَاقٌ"]," (K) and ↓ ",[2,"خَنْقٌ"],". (TA; and so, accord. to the TA, in the K.) You say, ",[2,"أَخَذْتُ"],[2,"بِمُخَنَّقِهِ"]," [",[1,"I seized his throat"],"]. (S.) And ",[2,"أَخَذَهُ"],[2,"بِمُخَنَّقِهِ"]," (K, accord. to the TA, but accord. to the CK and my MS. copy of the K ↓ ",[2,"بِمَخْنَقِهِ"],",) and ↓ ",[2,"بِخُنَاقِهِ"]," and ↓ ",[2,"بِخِنَاقِهِ"],", i. e. [",[1,"He took him,"]," or ",[1,"seized him,"],"] ",[1,"by his throat."]," (K.) And ",[2,"أَخَذَ بِمُخَنَّقِهِ"]," (A in art. ",[2,"زرد"],") and ↓ ",[2,"بِخُنَاقِهِ"]," (S) [properly ",[1,"He,"]," or ",[1,"it, seized his throat,"]," or ",[1,"throttled him,"]," or ",[1,"choked him;"]," meaning] (tropical:) ",[1,"he,"]," or ",[1,"it, straitened him;"]," as also ",[2,"أَخَذَ بِمُزَرَّدِهِ"],". (A in art. ",[2,"زرد"],".) And ",[2,"أَخَذَ مِنْهُ"],[2,"بِالمُخَنَّقِ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"He,"]," or ",[1,"it, constrained him,"]," and ",[1,"straitened him."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"بَلَغَ مِنْهُ المُخَنَّقَ"]," [properly ",[1,"It reached his throat;"]," meaning (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"it straitened him,"]," or ",[1,"distressed him"],"]. (S.) ",[2,"بَلَغَ الأَمْرُ المُخَنَّقَ"]," signifies the same as ",[2,"بَلَغَ المُذَمَّرَ"],", (A in art. ",[2,"ذمر"],",) which means (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The affair,"]," or ",[1,"case,"]," or ",[1,"event, reached a distressing pitch."]," (K in art. ",[2,"ذمر"],".)"]},{"h":"مَخْنُوقٌ","t":["and ↓ ",[2,"خَنِقٌ"]," and ↓ ",[2,"خَنِيقٌ"]," (JK, K) and ↓ ",[2,"خَانِقٌ"],", applied to a man, [and to any animal, as also ↓ ",[2,"مُخَنَّقٌ"],", ",[1,"Throttled,"]," or ",[1,"strangled,"]," i. e. ",[1,"having his throat squeezed that he may die;"]," but not always meaning, ",[1,"so as to be killed thereby;"]," often meaning, simply, ",[1,"throttled, strangled,"]," or ",[1,"choked;"],"] (JK;) all signify the same; from ",[2,"خَنَقَهُ"],": (JK, K:) or ↓ ",[2,"خَانِقٌ"],", in the place of ↓ ",[2,"خَنِيقٌ"],", signifies ",[2,"ذو خناق"]," [app. meaning having a ",[2,"خِنَاق"],", or ",[1,"cord,"]," &c., ",[1,"by which he is throttled,"]," or ",[1,"strangled, round his neck;"]," or perhaps ",[1,"having a"],[2,"خُنَاق"],", or ",[1,"quinsy"],"]: (TA:) and ↓ ",[2,"شَاةٌ خَنِيقَةٌ"]," and ↓ ",[2,"مُنْخَنِقَةٌ"]," signify ",[1,"a sheep,"]," or ",[1,"goat, throttled,"]," or ",[1,"strangled,"]," i. e. ",[1,"having its throat squeezed that it may die:"]," (Msb:) or the latter of these two means ",[1,"a sheep,"]," or ",[1,"goat, throttled,"]," or ",[1,"strangled,"]," or ",[1,"choked, by itself"]," (",[2,"اِنْخَتَقَتْ بِنَفْسِهَا"],"). (S, TA. [See 8.]) It is said in a prov., (Meyd,) ",[2,"اِفْتَدِ مَخْنُوقُ"],", (Meyd, K,) i. e. ",[2,"يَا مَخْنُوقُ"]," [",[1,"Ransom thyself, O"]," thou who art ",[1,"throttled,"]," or ",[1,"strangled,"]," or ",[1,"choked"],"]; applied to any one distressed and constrained; (Meyd;) meaning free thyself from difficulty (K, TA) and harm: (TA:) or, as some relate it, ",[2,"اِفْتَدَى مَخْنُوقٌ"]," [",[1,"One throttled,"]," or ",[1,"strangled,"]," or ",[1,"choked, ransomed himself"],"]. (Meyd.)"]},{"h":"مُخْتَنَقٌ","t":[[1,"A narrow place"]," or ",[1,"pass."]," (S, TA.) [See also ",[2,"خَانِقٌ"],", near the end of the paragraph.]"]},{"h":"مُخْتَنِقٌ","t":["(tropical:) A horse ",[1,"whose blaze occupies his jaws,"]," (K, TA,) ",[1,"extending to the roots of his ears."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"شَاةٌ مُنْخَنِقَةٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"مَخْنُوقٌ"],"."]}]},"maqayis":["الخاء والنون والقاف أصل واحد يدل على ضيق. فالخانق: الشعب الضيق. وقال بعض أهل العلم: إن أهل اليمن يسمون الزقاق خانقا. والخنق مصدر خنقه يخنقه خنقا. قال بعض أهل العلم: لا يقال خنقا. والمخنقة: القلادة."],"mufradat":["قوله تعالى: والمنخنقة [المائدة/ 3] ، أي: التي خنقت حتى ماتت، والمخنقة: القلادة."]}